is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
max-visits: 12

= Inter-Party Relationships

No party has won a majority on its own since 1957, and none will soon. Every government needs partners. Which relationships should we work on?

- @liberals: Strengthen our ties with the Grüne and the FDP.
- @center: Strengthen our ties with the CDU/CSU.
- @linke: Work on our relationship with the Linke.
- @bsw: Sound out the BSW.
- @spd_alone: The SPD can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard

@linke
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; linke_inter_party_seen += 1
go-to: linke_1 if linke_coalition_success = 0 and (linke_relation < 40 or linke_rectified_history = 1); linke_rectification_of_history if linke_relation >= 40 and linke_rectified_history = 0; linke_2 if linke_coalition_success >= 1 and linke_rectified_history = 1

@linke_1
on-arrival: linke_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); linke_coalition += 1 if linke_inter_party_seen <= 1; reformist_dissent += 2; cdu_relation -= 2; fdp_relation -= 3

The Linke's leaders are suspicious, but our members meet theirs at union events and in local councils, where SPD and Linke have governed together for years in Berlin, Bremen and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania.

@linke_rectification_of_history

One obstacle remains: the Linke was founded in protest against Agenda 2010 and the Hartz reforms of Gerhard Schröder's government. For many of its members, an SPD that does not break with that legacy cannot be trusted.

- @yes_history: Yes, we must admit that Hartz IV was a mistake.
- @no_history: No, the reforms were necessary at the time.

@yes_history
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 12; reformist_strength -= 2; center_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 6; left_strength += 5; linke_rectified_history = 1; cdu_relation -= 4; fdp_relation -= 6; linke_relation += 8*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 2*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if cdu_in_government or fdp_in_government

A party congress resolution says plainly that the Hartz reforms hurt millions of people and broke the trust of our voters. Gerhard Schröder's old allies are furious, and the business press calls it a turn to the left.

@no_history
on-arrival: linke_relation -= 3; reformist_dissent -= 3

We will not apologise for reforms that brought Germany out of mass unemployment.

@linke_2
on-arrival: linke_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); linke_coalition += 1 if linke_inter_party_seen <= 1; reformist_dissent += 2; cdu_relation -= 3; fdp_relation -= 3

After our successful time in government together, the Linke trusts us much more.

@center
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: center_op if cdu_in_government = 1 and spd_in_government = 0; center_coalition if spd_in_government = 1 and cdu_in_government = 1; center_other if cdu_in_government = 0

@center_op
on-arrival: cdu_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are in opposition to the Union's government, but that does not stop us from building goodwill.

@center_coalition
on-arrival: cdu_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

We govern together, so building trust comes naturally.

@center_other
on-arrival: cdu_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We keep in touch with the Union's leaders and its social wing, the CDA.

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; greens_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)
go-to: fdp_in if fdp_r >= 5; fdp_out if fdp_r < 5

The Grüne are our natural partners in most of the Länder.

@fdp_in
on-arrival: fdp_relation += 6*(1 - dissent)

The FDP has not forgotten the collapse of the traffic light in 2024, but its leaders are pragmatic.

@fdp_out
on-arrival: fdp_relation += 4*(1 - dissent)

The FDP is not in the Bundestag, so perhaps our efforts are best spent elsewhere. Still, it governs in some Länder, and may come back.

@bsw
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; bsw_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); reformist_dissent += 4; greens_relation -= 2

The BSW shares many of our social goals, but not our foreign policy. Our minister-president in Brandenburg has governed with it. The Seeheimer are not pleased.

@spd_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
